Client code throughout the application calls `Repository<Report> repo` and occasionally calls `repo.save(...)`, trusting the interface's declared behavior. Why is `ReadOnlyReportRepository` a Liskov Substitution Principle problem specifically, rather than just 'inheritance/interfaces are risky'?
